# React 18 + TypeScript Best Practices

## Project Conventions

- **Path alias**: `@/*` maps to `src/*`
- **UI library**: shadcn/ui (Radix + CVA + Tailwind) in `src/components/ui/`
- **State**: React Context for global state + TanStack Query v5 for server state
- **Forms**: react-hook-form + zod validation
- **Routing**: react-router-dom v6 with `/:lang` prefix for i18n
- **Icons**: lucide-react

## Component Patterns

### Functional Components with Props Interface

```typescript
interface ProductCardProps {
  product: Tables<"products">;
  onAddToCart?: (productId: string) => void;
  className?: string;
}

const ProductCard = ({ product, onAddToCart, className }: ProductCardProps) => {
  return (/* ... */);
};
```

### Export Conventions

- Named exports for utility components, hooks, contexts
- Default export for page components (required by React Router)
- Re-export hooks from their context files: `export const useCart = () => { ... }`

### Children Pattern

```typescript
interface LayoutProps {
  children: ReactNode;  // use ReactNode, not React.FC
}
```

## Hooks Best Practices

### Custom Hook Structure

```typescript
export function useProductData(productId: string) {
  // 1. All hooks at top level
  const queryClient = useQueryClient();
  const { toast } = useToast();

  // 2. Derived state with useMemo
  const isValid = useMemo(() => !!productId, [productId]);

  // 3. Callbacks with useCallback (stable references for child components)
  const refresh = useCallback(() => {
    queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ["product", productId] });
  }, [queryClient, productId]);

  // 4. Side effects last
  useEffect(() => { /* ... */ }, [productId]);

  // 5. Return typed object
  return { data, isLoading, refresh };
}
```

### When to Memoize

```typescript
// USE useMemo when: expensive computation or referential equality matters
const sortedItems = useMemo(
  () => items.sort((a, b) => a.price - b.price),
  [items]
);

// USE useCallback when: passing functions to memoized children or effect deps
const handleClick = useCallback((id: string) => {
  addToCart(id);
}, [addToCart]);

// DON'T memoize: simple values, primitive calculations, rarely-changing data
const count = items.length; // no memo needed
```

### Context Provider Pattern (project standard)

```typescript
interface CartContextType {
  cartItems: CartItem[];
  cartCount: number;
  addToCart: (productId: string, quantity?: number) => Promise<void>;
  // ... all methods
}

const CartContext = createContext<CartContextType | undefined>(undefined);

export const CartProvider = ({ children }: { children: ReactNode }) => {
  // State, callbacks, effects...

  // Memoize the context value to prevent unnecessary re-renders
  const value = useMemo(() => ({
    cartItems, cartCount, addToCart, removeItem, /* ... */
  }), [cartItems, cartCount, addToCart, removeItem]);

  return <CartContext.Provider value={value}>{children}</CartContext.Provider>;
};

// Safe consumer hook with error boundary
export const useCart = () => {
  const context = useContext(CartContext);
  if (context === undefined) {
    throw new Error("useCart must be used within a CartProvider");
  }
  return context;
};
```

## TypeScript Patterns

### Strict Typing Over `any`

```typescript
// AVOID any — use proper types
const handleSelect = (result: any) => { ... }  // bad

// USE specific types or generics
interface MapboxFeature {
  properties: {
    name: string;
    full_address?: string;
    context: FeatureContext;
  };
}
const handleSelect = (result: MapboxFeature) => { ... }  // good

// When type is truly unknown, use unknown + type guard
function processData(input: unknown): string {
  if (typeof input === "string") return input;
  if (typeof input === "object" && input !== null) return JSON.stringify(input);
  return String(input);
}
```

### Supabase Table Types

```typescript
import type { Tables, TablesInsert, TablesUpdate } from "@/integrations/supabase/types";

type Product = Tables<"products">;
type NewProduct = TablesInsert<"products">;
type ProductUpdate = TablesUpdate<"products">;
```

### Discriminated Unions for State

```typescript
type AsyncState<T> =
  | { status: "idle" }
  | { status: "loading" }
  | { status: "success"; data: T }
  | { status: "error"; error: Error };
```

### Zod Schema Integration

```typescript
import { z } from "zod";
import { zodResolver } from "@hookform/resolvers/zod";

const formSchema = z.object({
  name: z.string().min(2, "Name must be at least 2 characters"),
  email: z.string().email("Invalid email address"),
  price: z.coerce.number().positive("Price must be positive"),
});

type FormValues = z.infer<typeof formSchema>;

const form = useForm<FormValues>({
  resolver: zodResolver(formSchema),
  defaultValues: { name: "", email: "", price: 0 },
});
```

## Performance Patterns

### Code Splitting with Lazy Loading

```typescript
import { lazyLoad } from "@/utils/lazyLoad";

// Route-level splitting (pages)
const Shop = lazyLoad(() => import("@/pages/Shop"));
const AdminPage = lazyLoad(() => import("@/pages/account/AdminPage"));
```

### Avoid Re-renders in Lists

```typescript
// Memoize list items when parent re-renders frequently
const MemoizedProductCard = React.memo(ProductCard);

// Use stable keys — never use array index as key for dynamic lists
{products.map((product) => (
  <MemoizedProductCard key={product.id} product={product} />
))}
```

### Debounce User Input

```typescript
import { debounce } from "@/lib/utils";

// Debounce search/API calls triggered by user input
const debouncedSearch = useMemo(
  () => debounce((query: string) => handleAddressSearch(query, country), 300),
  [handleAddressSearch, country]
);
```

### Avoid Unnecessary State

```typescript
// WRONG — derived state in useState
const [fullName, setFullName] = useState("");
useEffect(() => {
  setFullName(`${firstName} ${lastName}`);
}, [firstName, lastName]);

// CORRECT — compute during render
const fullName = `${firstName} ${lastName}`;
```

## React Query Patterns (TanStack v5)

### Query Defaults (set in App.tsx)

```typescript
const queryClient = new QueryClient({
  defaultOptions: {
    queries: {
      staleTime: 5 * 60 * 1000,      // 5 min
      refetchOnWindowFocus: false,
      retry: 1,
    },
  },
});
```

### Query Keys Convention

```typescript
// Entity-based keys for predictable invalidation
["products"]                          // all products
["products", productId]               // single product
["products", "category", category]    // products by category
["cart", userId]                      // user's cart
["favorites", userId]                 // user's favorites
["profile", userId]                   // user profile
```

### Optimistic Updates

```typescript
const mutation = useMutation({
  mutationFn: updateProduct,
  onMutate: async (newData) => {
    await queryClient.cancelQueries({ queryKey: ["products", newData.id] });
    const previous = queryClient.getQueryData(["products", newData.id]);
    queryClient.setQueryData(["products", newData.id], newData);
    return { previous };
  },
  onError: (_err, _vars, context) => {
    queryClient.setQueryData(["products", context?.previous?.id], context?.previous);
  },
  onSettled: () => {
    queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ["products"] });
  },
});
```

## Error Handling

### Async/Await Pattern

```typescript
// Always wrap async operations with try/catch
const fetchData = async () => {
  try {
    const { data, error } = await supabase.from("products").select("*");
    if (error) throw error;
    return data;
  } catch (error) {
    console.error("Failed to fetch:", error);
    toast({ variant: "destructive", title: "Error", description: "Failed to load data" });
    throw error; // re-throw for React Query or parent to handle
  }
};
```

### Error Boundaries (for component tree errors)

```typescript
// Wrap critical sections with error boundaries
<ErrorBoundary fallback={<ErrorFallback />}>
  <ProductList />
</ErrorBoundary>
```

## Tailwind + shadcn/ui Conventions

```typescript
import { cn } from "@/lib/utils";
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button";
import { Card, CardHeader, CardTitle, CardContent } from "@/components/ui/card";

// Use cn() to merge conditional classes
<div className={cn("p-4 rounded-lg", isActive && "bg-primary/10", className)} />

// Use shadcn variants, don't reinvent
<Button variant="destructive" size="sm">Delete</Button>
```

## File Organization Rules

| Directory | Purpose | Naming |
|-----------|---------|--------|
| `src/pages/` | Route-level components | PascalCase, default export |
| `src/components/` | Reusable UI components | PascalCase |
| `src/components/ui/` | shadcn primitives (don't edit) | lowercase |
| `src/hooks/` | Custom hooks | `use` prefix, camelCase |
| `src/contexts/` | React Context providers | PascalCase + `Context` suffix |
| `src/lib/` | Pure utility functions | camelCase |
| `src/models/` | TypeScript type definitions | PascalCase |
| `src/integrations/` | Third-party API clients | lowercase directories |
